Lower the work, live-memory and reader-buffer budgets in --cfg fuzzing builds

kefir charges every checking step against WORK_CHARGED (2^48 units) and
every managed allocation against MANAGED_LIVE_BYTES (16 GiB); exhausting
either declines with a resource code. Under fuzzing an exec should end
in about a second and within wasmfuzz's 8-512 MiB memory cap, so the
fuzzing build uses 2^24 work units (the arena and nano-lean fixtures
charge at most 2.3M, 0.06 s natively) and 256 MiB. READER_BUFFER_BYTES
drops from 64 KiB to 4 KiB: the framer zero-fills the buffer on every
check, a byte loop at opt-level s that cost ~1.2M of the ~1.3M wasm
instructions of a header-only exec. The reported resource_profile
identity is computed by build.rs, which does not see the cfg on cross
builds, so it still names the production profile.
Upstream: none (issues disabled upstream, no PRs, checked 2026-11-22).

